    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first builds a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into tokens without dropping them.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field. That field is the carrier that super-resolution needs. The window operator partitions the carrier into tokens while keeping every token in the expression.",
